# Qin et al. (2025), PASA 42, e049 (arXiv:2412.00799; the published Table A1 equals arXiv Table 3): ionizing emissivity Ndot_ion, NOT tabulated in the
#   paper: read from the vector figures. Value = the MAP model ("w/ rec", red) of Fig. 8 (lower left); bounds = the 68% band
#   of Fig. 6 (the inner of its two red bands; the 95% band is not stored). Checks: the Gamma and MFP MAP curves of Fig. 8 match
#   Table A1 (Gamma to its rounding, MFP within 2.4%) and x_HI too; Kulkarni+19 as drawn in Fig. 6 matches Kulkarni+19 Fig. 1
#   within 0.010 dex. z = the model redshift grid, z <= 12 (the range of Fig. 8).
#   Posterior of a 21cmFAST-based model forward-modelling the XQR-30+ Lya forest (tau_eff distributions at z = 5.3-6.1), with
#   the UV LFs (z = 6-10) and the Planck CMB optical depth in the likelihood (fiducial model); model-based, so the z > 6 values are
#   constrained mostly through the model, not measured. Cosmology of the 21cmFAST runs not stated (values in physical units).
#   The MAP (a single model, jagged) lies outside the 68% band at 9 of these redshifts, by up to 0.015 dex (z = 5.78).
#   Fig. 6 and 8 vector paths: papers folder Qin2025_2412.00799/src/figs/post_emissivity{,_rec}.pdf.
